IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `tas-nouns`
IMPORT `tas-interpretation-time`

-- Acts Interpretation Act 1931 (Tasmania), ss 8 to 10A: amending Acts, purpose, extrinsic material, commencement, evidence of commencement, "must", "is to" and "may".
-- Answers of a rule of reading: JUST TRUE where the text applies to the case; JUST FALSE only where the text itself says no to the case in its own words
--   (a "means" definition, a condition introduced with "if", "only if", "as long as" or "unless", a list closed with "only", a flat negative, a "where" that fails, a period the text fixes and the case falls outside it);
-- NOTHING everywhere else (an open list, "includes", a term left undefined, silence, a pointer outside the sources, a grant or prohibition limited by its own wording where the case falls outside the limit, a scope limit with no "only").
-- A rule that returns a day, a name or a value has no second not-covered answer, so it returns NOTHING when its text does not apply.
-- The arithmetic of s 9 (the day, and the moment within the day) is in tas-interpretation-time.l4; this module chooses between its rules.

§ `s 8: Acts amending other Acts`

-- src:113 | (1) Every Act passed for the purpose and with the object of amending a previous Act shall be read and construed with, and subject to the provisions of, the amended Act, as modified by the amending Act, and shall be deemed to be incorporated therewith, and with every Act amending the same, unless the contrary is expressly provided therein.
@ref s 8(1) (src:113)
GIVEN `passed for the purpose and with the object of amending a previous Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is expressly provided in the amending Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(1): an amending Act is read and construed with the amended Act and deemed to be incorporated with it` `passed for the purpose and with the object of amending a previous Act` `the contrary is expressly provided in the amending Act` MEANS
    IF NOT (`passed for the purpose and with the object of amending a previous Act`)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (NOT (`the contrary is expressly provided in the amending Act`))

-- The series of Acts upon the same subject is given in the order in which they were passed, earliest first.
-- src:115 | (2) Where any Act is amended as aforesaid, the expression
-- src:117 | the Principal Act in any such amending Act, unless the contrary is expressly provided, shall mean the Act so amended, and shall be deemed to apply to the earliest of the series of Acts upon the same subject, even though the amendment consists only of some alteration in, or modification of, a previous amending Act.
@ref s 8(2) (src:115-117)
GIVEN `the series of Acts upon the same subject, earliest first` IS A LIST OF STRING
      `the contrary is expressly provided` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 8(2): the Act that the expression the Principal Act means in an amending Act` `the series of Acts upon the same subject, earliest first` `the contrary is expressly provided` MEANS
    IF `the contrary is expressly provided`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER `the series of Acts upon the same subject, earliest first`
         WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
         WHEN earliest FOLLOWED BY later THEN JUST earliest

#ASSERT `s 8(1): an amending Act is read and construed with the amended Act and deemed to be incorporated with it` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 8(1): an amending Act is read and construed with the amended Act and deemed to be incorporated with it` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 8(1): an amending Act is read and construed with the amended Act and deemed to be incorporated with it` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 8(2): the Act that the expression the Principal Act means in an amending Act` (LIST "Widgets Act 1950", "Widgets Amendment Act 1960", "Widgets Amendment Act 1970") FALSE EQUALS JUST "Widgets Act 1950"
#ASSERT `s 8(2): the Act that the expression the Principal Act means in an amending Act` (LIST "Widgets Act 1950", "Widgets Amendment Act 1960") TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 8(2): the Act that the expression the Principal Act means in an amending Act` EMPTY FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 8A: the purpose or object of an Act`

DECLARE `Which of two interpretations` IS ONE OF
    `the first interpretation`
    `the second interpretation`

-- src:121 | (1) In the interpretation of a provision of an Act, an interpretation that promotes the purpose or object of the Act is to be preferred to an interpretation that does not promote the purpose or object.
@ref s 8A(1) (src:121)
GIVEN `the first interpretation promotes the purpose or object of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the second interpretation promotes the purpose or object of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Which of two interpretations`
`s 8A(1): the interpretation that is to be preferred` `the first interpretation promotes the purpose or object of the Act` `the second interpretation promotes the purpose or object of the Act` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the first interpretation promotes the purpose or object of the Act` AND NOT (`the second interpretation promotes the purpose or object of the Act`) THEN JUST `the first interpretation`
           IF `the second interpretation promotes the purpose or object of the Act` AND NOT (`the first interpretation promotes the purpose or object of the Act`) THEN JUST `the second interpretation`
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:123 | (2) Subsection (1) applies whether or not the purpose or object is expressly stated in the Act.
@ref s 8A(2) (src:123)
GIVEN `the purpose or object is expressly stated in the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 8A(2): subsection (1) applies` `the purpose or object is expressly stated in the Act` MEANS TRUE

#ASSERT `s 8A(1): the interpretation that is to be preferred` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the first interpretation`
#ASSERT `s 8A(1): the interpretation that is to be preferred` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST `the second interpretation`
#ASSERT `s 8A(1): the interpretation that is to be preferred` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 8A(1): the interpretation that is to be preferred` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 8A(2): subsection (1) applies` TRUE
#ASSERT `s 8A(2): subsection (1) applies` FALSE

§ `s 8B: extrinsic material`

DECLARE `Purpose of considering extrinsic material` IS ONE OF
    `to provide an interpretation of an ambiguous or obscure provision`
    `to provide an interpretation that avoids a manifestly absurd or unreasonable result`
    `to confirm the interpretation conveyed by the ordinary meaning`

-- src:127 | (1) Subject to subsection (2), in the interpretation of a provision of an Act, consideration may be given to extrinsic material capable of assisting in the interpretation –
-- src:129 | (a) if the provision is ambiguous or obscure, to provide an interpretation of it; or
-- src:131 | (b) if the ordinary meaning of the provision leads to a result that is manifestly absurd or is unreasonable, to provide an interpretation that avoids such a result; or
-- src:133 | (c) in any other case, to confirm the interpretation conveyed by the ordinary meaning of the provision.
@ref s 8B(1) (src:127-133)
GIVEN `the material is capable of assisting in the interpretation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision is ambiguous or obscure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the ordinary meaning of the provision leads to a result that is manifestly absurd or is unreasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF `Purpose of considering extrinsic material`)
`s 8B(1): consideration may be given to extrinsic material, for these purposes` `the material is capable of assisting in the interpretation` `the provision is ambiguous or obscure` `the ordinary meaning of the provision leads to a result that is manifestly absurd or is unreasonable` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the material is capable of assisting in the interpretation`)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE BRANCH IF `the provision is ambiguous or obscure` AND `the ordinary meaning of the provision leads to a result that is manifestly absurd or is unreasonable`
                THEN JUST (LIST `to provide an interpretation of an ambiguous or obscure provision`, `to provide an interpretation that avoids a manifestly absurd or unreasonable result`)
                IF `the provision is ambiguous or obscure` THEN JUST (LIST `to provide an interpretation of an ambiguous or obscure provision`)
                IF `the ordinary meaning of the provision leads to a result that is manifestly absurd or is unreasonable` THEN JUST (LIST `to provide an interpretation that avoids a manifestly absurd or unreasonable result`)
                OTHERWISE JUST (LIST `to confirm the interpretation conveyed by the ordinary meaning`)

-- src:135 | (2) In determining whether consideration should be given to extrinsic material, and in determining the weight to be given to extrinsic material, regard is to be given to –
-- src:137 | (a) the desirability of a provision being interpreted as having its ordinary meaning; and
-- src:139 | (b) the undesirability of prolonging legal or other proceedings without compensating advantage; and
-- src:141 | (c) other relevant matters.
@ref s 8B(2) (src:135-141)
`s 8B(2): the matters to which regard is to be given in deciding whether and how far to consider extrinsic material` MEANS LIST
    "the desirability of a provision being interpreted as having its ordinary meaning"
  , "the undesirability of prolonging legal or other proceedings without compensating advantage"
  , "other relevant matters"

DECLARE `Kind of material outside the text of an Act` IS ONE OF
    `material set out in the document containing the text of the Act as printed by the Government Printer`
    `a relevant report of a Royal Commission, Law Reform Commission or Commissioner, board or committee of inquiry, or a similar body, laid before either House before the provision was enacted`
    `a relevant report of a committee of Parliament or of either House made to Parliament or that House before the provision was enacted`
    `a treaty or other international agreement mentioned in the Act`
    `an explanatory note, clause note or memorandum relating to the Bill, or other relevant document, laid before or made available to the members of either House before the provision was enacted`
    `the speech made to a House by a member in moving that the Bill be read a second time`
    `relevant material in the Votes and Proceedings of either House or in any official record of debates`
    `a document declared by an Act to be a relevant document for the purposes of s 8B`
    `other material`

-- src:145 | extrinsic material in relation to a provision of an Act, means material not forming part of the Act, including –
-- src:147 | (a) material that is set out in the document containing the text of the Act as printed by the Government Printer; and
-- src:149 | (b) a relevant report of a Royal Commission, Law Reform Commission or Commissioner, board or committee of inquiry, or a similar body, that was laid before either House of Parliament before the provision concerned was enacted; and
-- src:151 | (c) a relevant report of a committee of Parliament or of either House of Parliament that was made to Parliament or that House of Parliament before the provision was enacted; and
-- src:153 | (d) a treaty or other international agreement that is mentioned in the Act; and
-- src:155 | (e) any explanatory note, clause note or memorandum relating to the Bill that contained the provision, or any other relevant document, that was laid before, or given or otherwise made available to the members of, either House of Parliament by the member bringing in the Bill before the provision was enacted; and
-- src:157 | (f) the speech made to a House of Parliament by a member of the House in moving a motion that the Bill be read a second time; and
-- src:159 | (g) relevant material in the Votes and Proceedings of either House of Parliament or in any official record of debates in Parliament or either House of Parliament; and
-- src:161 | (h) a document that is declared by an Act to be a relevant document for the purposes of this section;
@ref s 8B(3) (src:145-161)
GIVEN `the material` IS A `Kind of material outside the text of an Act`
      `the material forms part of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 8B(3): the material is extrinsic material in relation to a provision of an Act` `the material` `the material forms part of the Act` MEANS
    IF `the material` EQUALS `other material`
    THEN NOT (`the material forms part of the Act`)
    ELSE TRUE

#ASSERT `s 8B(1): consideration may be given to extrinsic material, for these purposes` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST (LIST `to provide an interpretation of an ambiguous or obscure provision`)
#ASSERT `s 8B(1): consideration may be given to extrinsic material, for these purposes` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST (LIST `to provide an interpretation that avoids a manifestly absurd or unreasonable result`)
#ASSERT `s 8B(1): consideration may be given to extrinsic material, for these purposes` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST (LIST `to provide an interpretation of an ambiguous or obscure provision`, `to provide an interpretation that avoids a manifestly absurd or unreasonable result`)
#ASSERT `s 8B(1): consideration may be given to extrinsic material, for these purposes` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST (LIST `to confirm the interpretation conveyed by the ordinary meaning`)
#ASSERT `s 8B(1): consideration may be given to extrinsic material, for these purposes` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT count `s 8B(2): the matters to which regard is to be given in deciding whether and how far to consider extrinsic material` EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `s 8B(3): the material is extrinsic material in relation to a provision of an Act` `a treaty or other international agreement mentioned in the Act` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 8B(3): the material is extrinsic material in relation to a provision of an Act` `material set out in the document containing the text of the Act as printed by the Government Printer` TRUE
#ASSERT `s 8B(3): the material is extrinsic material in relation to a provision of an Act` `the speech made to a House by a member in moving that the Bill be read a second time` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 8B(3): the material is extrinsic material in relation to a provision of an Act` `other material` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 8B(3): the material is extrinsic material in relation to a provision of an Act` `other material` TRUE)

§ `s 9: commencement`

-- s 9(1) is shown only as a row of dots. The rules of ss 9(2) to (5) are in tas-interpretation-time.l4; this rule chooses between them.
-- The caller states whether the Act reserved for the signification of the Sovereign's pleasure, and which of the days applies.
-- src:169 | (2) Every Act to which the Royal Assent has been given by the Governor for or on behalf of the Sovereign before the commencement of section 8 of the Acts Interpretation Amendment Act 1981 shall, unless the contrary intention appears in the first-mentioned Act, be deemed to have come into operation on the day on which that Act received the Royal Assent.
-- src:171 | (3) Every Act to which the Royal Assent is given by the Governor for and on behalf of the Sovereign on or after the date of commencement of section 8 of the Acts Interpretation Amendment Act 1981 shall, unless the contrary intention appears in the first-mentioned Act, come into operation on the fourteenth day after the day on which that Act receives the Royal Assent.
-- src:173 | (3A) Despite subsection (3), if a provision of an Act provides that the Act or a portion of the Act commences on a day, or a day or days, to be proclaimed, that provision and the provision providing for the short title of the Act come into operation on the day on which the Act receives the Royal Assent unless the Act expressly provides otherwise.
-- src:175 | (4) Every Act reserved for the signification of the Sovereign's pleasure after the commencement of section 8 of the Acts Interpretation Amendment Act 1981 shall, unless the contrary intention appears in that Act, come into operation on the day after the day on which a proclamation of the Governor signifying the Sovereign's assent is published or notified in the Gazette.
@ref s 9(2), (3), (3A) and (4) (src:169-175)
GIVEN `the day of Royal Assent` IS A DATE
      `the Act was reserved for the signification of the Sovereign's pleasure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day it was reserved` IS A DATE
      `the day the proclamation signifying the Sovereign's assent was published or notified in the Gazette` IS A DATE
      `the day section 8 of the 1981 Amendment Act commenced` IS A DATE
      `the Act shows a contrary intention` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Act provides for commencement on a day or days to be proclaimed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 9: the day on which an Act as a whole comes into operation` `the day of Royal Assent` `the Act was reserved for the signification of the Sovereign's pleasure` `the day it was reserved` `the day the proclamation signifying the Sovereign's assent was published or notified in the Gazette` `the day section 8 of the 1981 Amendment Act commenced` `the Act shows a contrary intention` `the Act provides for commencement on a day or days to be proclaimed` MEANS
    IF `the Act provides for commencement on a day or days to be proclaimed`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the Act was reserved for the signification of the Sovereign's pleasure`
         THEN `s 9(4): the day an Act reserved for the signification of the Sovereign's pleasure comes into operation` `the day the proclamation signifying the Sovereign's assent was published or notified in the Gazette` `after reservation on` `the day it was reserved` `with` `the day section 8 of the 1981 Amendment Act commenced` `and` `the Act shows a contrary intention`
         ELSE IF `the day of Royal Assent` BELOW `the day section 8 of the 1981 Amendment Act commenced`
              THEN `s 9(2): the day an Act assented to before the commencement of section 8 of the 1981 Amendment Act is deemed to have come into operation` `the day of Royal Assent` `with` `the day section 8 of the 1981 Amendment Act commenced` `and` `the Act shows a contrary intention`
              ELSE `s 9(3): the day an Act assented to on or after the commencement of section 8 of the 1981 Amendment Act comes into operation` `the day of Royal Assent` `with` `the day section 8 of the 1981 Amendment Act commenced` `and` `the Act shows a contrary intention`

-- Fixture: section 8 of the 1981 Amendment Act is taken to have commenced on 1 January 1982; the deposited text does not state the day.
#ASSERT `s 9: the day on which an Act as a whole comes into operation` (Date 10 3 1990) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1982) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 24 3 1990)
#ASSERT `s 9: the day on which an Act as a whole comes into operation` (Date 18 1 1932) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1982) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 18 1 1932)
#ASSERT `s 9: the day on which an Act as a whole comes into operation` (Date 10 3 1990) TRUE (Date 1 6 1990) (Date 20 6 1990) (Date 1 1 1982) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 21 6 1990)
#ASSERT `s 9: the day on which an Act as a whole comes into operation` (Date 10 3 1990) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1982) FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 9: the day on which an Act as a whole comes into operation` (Date 10 3 1990) FALSE (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1900) (Date 1 1 1982) TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- src:177 | (5) Where an Act, or a regulation or other instrument or document made, issued, or granted under an Act, is expressed to commence, come into operation, or take effect on a particular day, it shall commence, come into operation, or take effect immediately on the expiration of the last preceding day.
@ref s 9(5) (src:177)
GIVEN `the day it is expressed to commence, come into operation or take effect on` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Moment in a day`
`s 9(5): the moment an Act or instrument expressed to commence on a day takes effect` `the day it is expressed to commence, come into operation or take effect on` MEANS
    `s 9(5): the moment at which an Act or instrument expressed to commence on a day takes effect` `the day it is expressed to commence, come into operation or take effect on`

#ASSERT `s 9(5): the moment an Act or instrument expressed to commence on a day takes effect` (Date 1 7 2026) EQUALS `Moment in a day` OF (Date 1 7 2026), `the first moment of the day`

§ `s 10: evidence of commencement`

-- src:179 | 10. Evidence of commencement
-- src:181 | The date appearing on the copy of an Act produced under section 6(10) of the Legislation Publication Act 1996 and purporting to be the date on which the Governor assented thereto, or made known the Sovereign's assent thereto, shall be evidence that such date was the date on which the Governor so assented or made known such assent, and shall be judicially noticed.
@ref s 10 (src:179-181)
GIVEN `the copy was produced under section 6(10) of the Legislation Publication Act 1996` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date purports to be the date on which the Governor assented or made known the Sovereign's assent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10: the date on the copy is evidence of the date of assent and is judicially noticed` `the copy was produced under section 6(10) of the Legislation Publication Act 1996` `the date purports to be the date on which the Governor assented or made known the Sovereign's assent` MEANS
    IF `the copy was produced under section 6(10) of the Legislation Publication Act 1996` AND `the date purports to be the date on which the Governor assented or made known the Sovereign's assent`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 10: the date on the copy is evidence of the date of assent and is judicially noticed` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 10: the date on the copy is evidence of the date of assent and is judicially noticed` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 10: the date on the copy is evidence of the date of assent and is judicially noticed` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 10A: "must", "is to" and "may"`

DECLARE `Word of obligation or permission` IS ONE OF
    `must`
    `is to`
    `are to`
    `may`

DECLARE `Construction of a word of obligation or permission` IS ONE OF
    `construed as being mandatory`
    `construed as being directory`
    `construed as being discretionary or enabling, as the context requires`

-- src:185 | (1) In any Act –
-- src:187 | (a) the word "must" is to be construed as being mandatory; and
-- src:189 | (b) the words "is to" and "are to" are to be construed as being directory; and
-- src:191 | (c) the word "may" is to be construed as being discretionary or enabling, as the context requires.
@ref s 10A(1) (src:185-191)
GIVEN word IS A `Word of obligation or permission`
GIVETH A `Construction of a word of obligation or permission`
`s 10A(1): how the word is construed` word MEANS
    CONSIDER word
    WHEN `must` THEN `construed as being mandatory`
    WHEN `is to` THEN `construed as being directory`
    WHEN `are to` THEN `construed as being directory`
    WHEN `may` THEN `construed as being discretionary or enabling, as the context requires`

-- src:193 | (2) Subsection (1) applies only in respect of a provision of an Act if that provision is passed after the commencement of the Justice Legislation (Miscellaneous Amendments) Act 2000.
@ref s 10A(2) (src:193)
GIVEN `the provision was passed after the commencement of the Justice Legislation (Miscellaneous Amendments) Act 2000` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 10A(2): subsection (1) applies in respect of the provision` `the provision was passed after the commencement of the Justice Legislation (Miscellaneous Amendments) Act 2000` MEANS
    `the provision was passed after the commencement of the Justice Legislation (Miscellaneous Amendments) Act 2000`

-- src:185 | (1) In any Act –
-- src:187 | (a) the word "must" is to be construed as being mandatory; and
-- src:189 | (b) the words "is to" and "are to" are to be construed as being directory; and
-- src:191 | (c) the word "may" is to be construed as being discretionary or enabling, as the context requires.
-- src:193 | (2) Subsection (1) applies only in respect of a provision of an Act if that provision is passed after the commencement of the Justice Legislation (Miscellaneous Amendments) Act 2000.
@ref s 10A(1) and (2) (src:185-193)
GIVEN word IS A `Word of obligation or permission`
      `the provision was passed after the commencement of the Justice Legislation (Miscellaneous Amendments) Act 2000` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE (`Construction of a word of obligation or permission`)
`s 10A: the construction of the word in the provision` word `the provision was passed after the commencement of the Justice Legislation (Miscellaneous Amendments) Act 2000` MEANS
    IF `s 10A(2): subsection (1) applies in respect of the provision` `the provision was passed after the commencement of the Justice Legislation (Miscellaneous Amendments) Act 2000`
    THEN JUST (`s 10A(1): how the word is construed` word)
    ELSE NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 10A(1): how the word is construed` `must` EQUALS `construed as being mandatory`
#ASSERT `s 10A(1): how the word is construed` `is to` EQUALS `construed as being directory`
#ASSERT `s 10A(1): how the word is construed` `are to` EQUALS `construed as being directory`
#ASSERT `s 10A(1): how the word is construed` `may` EQUALS `construed as being discretionary or enabling, as the context requires`
#ASSERT `s 10A(2): subsection (1) applies in respect of the provision` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 10A(2): subsection (1) applies in respect of the provision` FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 10A: the construction of the word in the provision` `must` TRUE EQUALS JUST `construed as being mandatory`
#ASSERT `s 10A: the construction of the word in the provision` `must` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
